WEBVTT

00:00:03.710 --> 00:00:04.250
A-chan!

00:00:04.660 --> 00:00:05.560
Welcome back!

00:00:06.410 --> 00:00:07.030
I'm back!

00:00:07.510 --> 00:00:09.020
It's been a while!

00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:10.940
How was Florida?

00:00:11.420 --> 00:00:12.360
Did you have fun?

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:14.390
Yeah, it was fun.

00:00:14.890 --> 00:00:16.330
W-what?

00:00:16.570 --> 00:00:18.160
You haven't changed much.

00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:21.370
You don't look any different in two weeks.

00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:23.390
Oh, you're famous.

00:00:23.850 --> 00:00:24.350
Coach Aoi!

00:00:24.830 --> 00:00:27.120
Thanks to you, I had a great experience.

00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:29.470
I don't need to thank you for that.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.840
You've gotten stronger, haven't you?

00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:34.070
Yes, I have.

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:10.000
His form has become smoother without any unnecessary effort.

00:02:10.520 --> 00:02:12.970
It's proof that he came back with confidence.

00:02:13.530 --> 00:02:16.190
It was the right decision to let him go to America.

00:02:16.450 --> 00:02:19.400
But to be honest, it's still tough to win the All Japan Junior Championship.

00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:24.350
I know. But that's his goal.

00:02:24.810 --> 00:02:28.840
If you think about it, he's not as good as Maruo, who has a narrow career.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.220
That's why I called you.

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:34.880
I'll do whatever I can, though.

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:39.160
Two and a half months until the Kanagawa Junior Tennis Tournament.

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:44.280
From tomorrow, Yukichi will increase the normal menu and the strength-enhancing menu.

00:02:45.940 --> 00:02:47.270
Y-Yes!

00:02:47.650 --> 00:02:52.920
Maruo will increase the body-modification menu and the attack-control menu in Florida.

00:02:53.300 --> 00:02:57.040
Other than that, he will also increase the special menu, so keep that in mind.

00:02:57.360 --> 00:02:57.720
Yes!

00:02:57.880 --> 00:02:59.820
Two months is too short.

00:02:59.820 --> 00:02:59.980
Thank you very much.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:01.820
You can't waste even a second.

00:03:03.440 --> 00:03:03.900
Yes!

00:03:04.380 --> 00:03:16.580
Your ball is heavier than before.

00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:17.760
Really?

00:03:18.520 --> 00:03:20.180
It's one of the things I learned in Florida.

00:03:20.860 --> 00:03:22.330
Ei-chan, sorry to keep you waiting.

00:03:22.470 --> 00:03:22.690
Yeah.

00:03:24.780 --> 00:03:26.610
See you later!

00:03:27.480 --> 00:03:28.080
See you tomorrow!

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:29.300
Good work!

00:03:31.150 --> 00:03:32.240
It's cold. Do you want to take the bus home?

00:03:32.620 --> 00:03:35.060
Yeah, let's walk home. I want to hear about Florida.

00:03:36.420 --> 00:03:37.970
Hey, didn't you see Natsu?

00:03:38.960 --> 00:03:40.300
I went home with my brother.

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:42.300
Maruoto?

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:45.440
Recently, my brother and Natsu have been getting along well.

00:03:46.300 --> 00:03:50.450
What are you talking about, Guma?

00:03:53.470 --> 00:03:55.270
You've gotten really good at it.

00:03:55.610 --> 00:03:56.150
Really?

00:03:56.860 --> 00:03:58.240
I'm so glad.

00:04:00.760 --> 00:04:04.030
I-It's been a while, and I feel like I'm going to cry...

00:04:04.030 --> 00:04:06.400
Hey, so? Did you have trouble with your overseas life?

00:04:08.260 --> 00:04:12.960
Oh, there was a Japanese guy named Atsushi-san, and he helped me with a lot of things, so I was fine.

00:04:13.400 --> 00:04:16.740
I see. Everyone was worried that A-chan would do well over there.

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:20.940
Like, you were too serious and couldn't get along with him.

00:04:21.940 --> 00:04:28.660
Ahaha. Well, it wasn't always fun, but I got a habit of losing, so I couldn't win at all.

00:04:30.280 --> 00:04:31.990
Losing habit? What's that?

00:04:32.410 --> 00:04:34.230
Eh? You don't have any experience?

00:04:34.690 --> 00:04:37.740
I see. You seem to be thinking too deeply.

00:04:40.290 --> 00:04:43.050
I'm thinking deeply too!

00:04:43.570 --> 00:04:45.940
Ah, no, that's not what I meant.

00:04:46.480 --> 00:04:48.100
I was wondering if there was a way to escape from thinking deeply.

00:04:50.460 --> 00:04:51.840
I think it's amazing.

00:04:52.640 --> 00:04:55.360
Hmm, well, that's fine. So?

00:04:55.780 --> 00:04:58.480
Oh, I played a match with Ike-kun over there.

00:04:58.480 --> 00:04:59.980
I was wondering if I could ask Ike-kun to...

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:01.180
I was told to say thanks to Natsu.

00:05:02.560 --> 00:05:05.120
You were helping me with something, weren't you?

00:05:05.610 --> 00:05:07.210
Oh, I don't know what you're talking about.

00:05:07.550 --> 00:05:09.170
Eh? Didn't you ask Ike-kun for something?

00:05:10.550 --> 00:05:12.070
I already forgot.

00:05:12.750 --> 00:05:14.370
You definitely remember that, don't you?

00:05:14.650 --> 00:05:15.870
I don't know.

00:05:16.890 --> 00:05:18.270
Well, it's okay.

00:05:18.510 --> 00:05:20.880
Thanks to you, I had a really good experience.

00:05:21.420 --> 00:05:22.680
Thank you.

00:05:23.340 --> 00:05:23.720
Yeah.

00:05:23.900 --> 00:05:25.040
How was it going, Sou-chan?

00:05:26.120 --> 00:05:28.240
Not only was I doing well, but I was already overwhelmed.

00:05:29.080 --> 00:05:29.920
My spirit...

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:31.460
What did you do?

00:05:31.740 --> 00:05:32.640
What did you do?

00:05:33.020 --> 00:05:34.730
I heard that Na-chan was engaged.

00:05:35.970 --> 00:05:36.290
Me?

00:05:36.890 --> 00:05:37.950
So-chan's?

00:05:38.250 --> 00:05:40.540
You believed me, didn't you?

00:05:40.720 --> 00:05:42.590
It's not a lie.

00:05:43.230 --> 00:05:43.870
What?

00:05:44.420 --> 00:05:44.660
What?

00:05:44.920 --> 00:05:47.060
Of course, it's a story from my childhood.

00:05:47.740 --> 00:05:50.000
When I grow up, I'm going to be So-chan's wife.

00:05:50.680 --> 00:05:51.920
It's a common thing.

00:05:52.730 --> 00:05:53.470
That's not good.

00:05:54.470 --> 00:05:57.370
The boy who was closest to me was So-chan.

00:05:58.150 --> 00:05:59.550
I don't understand the meaning of marriage.

00:05:59.550 --> 00:05:59.970
Thank you for watching.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:02.420
Even though I don't know much about it, I keep saying things like that.

00:06:02.720 --> 00:06:05.380
Even when I was in middle school, we were the best friends.

00:06:05.600 --> 00:06:07.800
At this rate, I thought it might really be like that.

00:06:09.560 --> 00:06:12.460
Middle school is relatively recent, isn't it?

00:06:12.990 --> 00:06:14.710
I somehow understood when I went to America.

00:06:16.830 --> 00:06:20.780
It's not about love, but my best friend comes to me.

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:26.670
Could it be that you're burning yaki mochi?

00:06:26.670 --> 00:06:27.150
Do you bake bread at home?

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:31.500
Of course I'll cry!

00:06:31.500 --> 00:06:32.880
Oh, I see.

00:06:37.800 --> 00:06:44.980
I've been thinking about it for a long time, but I still think about you.

00:06:50.910 --> 00:06:54.280
Mr. Bear.

00:07:18.240 --> 00:07:22.540
I feel like I'm on the net with a perfect chance ball that I can't decide.

00:07:23.300 --> 00:07:28.480
I did my best. I should have moved forward one step, no, half a step.

00:07:28.760 --> 00:07:29.780
Don't be in a hurry.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:30.840
Don't be in a hurry!

00:07:35.460 --> 00:07:37.420
He's surprisingly fast.

00:07:38.600 --> 00:07:40.220
As I thought, about Nacchan...

00:07:40.220 --> 00:07:43.020
That bastard.

00:07:43.850 --> 00:07:44.830
We've been dating for 10 years.

00:07:49.200 --> 00:07:49.840
Game set.

00:07:50.020 --> 00:07:51.000
Won by Egawa.

00:07:51.140 --> 00:07:57.490
I'm glad I won today.

00:08:00.030 --> 00:08:01.250
Takuma Egawa is the winner.

00:08:02.050 --> 00:08:04.270
Rike Souji is no longer fit for the domestic market.

00:08:05.070 --> 00:08:12.140
Are you ready to practice?

00:08:12.300 --> 00:08:12.900
Huh?

00:08:13.380 --> 00:08:15.130
You're getting better, aren't you?

00:08:15.130 --> 00:08:16.330
You said you were going to be a professional.

00:08:16.910 --> 00:08:27.690
You haven't been practicing much lately.

00:08:27.930 --> 00:08:29.720
Coach Miura is really good.

00:08:30.190 --> 00:08:30.990
I'm worried, too.

00:08:32.940 --> 00:08:36.680
Takuma!

00:08:37.260 --> 00:08:38.100
Takuma!

00:08:39.060 --> 00:08:42.280
You're okay, aren't you?

00:08:42.420 --> 00:08:42.920
Yeah.

00:08:43.620 --> 00:08:47.020
I'm going to the same high school as Takuma.

00:08:47.700 --> 00:08:50.540
Then call me Takuma-senpai from now on.

00:08:50.980 --> 00:08:52.500
I can't do it anymore.

00:08:52.820 --> 00:08:55.070
I'm Takuma, just like before.

00:08:55.250 --> 00:08:57.320
I went to practice because there was a summer who worried about me.

00:09:00.540 --> 00:09:05.300
It was fun just to hit the serve, but I was still running away from becoming a professional.

00:09:06.080 --> 00:09:09.240
Will I run away again without doing anything?

00:09:09.840 --> 00:09:10.220
No.

00:09:11.260 --> 00:09:17.140
What do you think?

00:09:17.390 --> 00:09:17.610
Fast!

00:09:42.410 --> 00:09:43.940
I'm out. I'm 20 years old.

00:09:44.300 --> 00:09:47.910
I made a mistake again.

00:09:48.970 --> 00:09:51.330
I know how hard it is for you guys to die.

00:09:52.910 --> 00:09:57.980
But the only time you can keep up with your body is two months before the match.

00:09:58.840 --> 00:09:59.820
Am I crazy?

00:10:00.480 --> 00:10:01.240
I'll stop you.

00:10:01.640 --> 00:10:03.860
So try as hard as you can.

00:10:03.960 --> 00:10:04.500
Yes!

00:10:05.270 --> 00:10:05.490
Yes!

00:10:06.330 --> 00:10:08.460
It's a practice match in the afternoon,

00:10:08.460 --> 00:10:10.700
but Maruo-kun, ask the opponent yourself.

00:10:11.960 --> 00:10:12.740
Ask him.

00:10:13.160 --> 00:10:15.060
Takuma-san?

00:10:15.900 --> 00:10:16.380
But...

00:10:16.380 --> 00:10:18.520
I was rejected by him before...

00:10:19.060 --> 00:10:19.900
Is that okay with you forever?

00:10:21.220 --> 00:10:24.630
What's your schedule?

00:10:25.190 --> 00:10:26.260
Um, excuse me!

00:10:26.500 --> 00:10:28.570
I have something to talk to Takuma-san.

00:10:29.110 --> 00:10:29.970
Maruo-kun...

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:33.670
Oh, I have something I want to ask you too.

00:10:33.830 --> 00:10:35.320
Come here for a moment.

00:10:35.360 --> 00:10:42.820
Eh? Um...

00:10:42.820 --> 00:10:43.360
Hey, you.

00:10:43.460 --> 00:10:43.740
Eh?

00:10:44.580 --> 00:10:44.800
Ah...

00:10:44.800 --> 00:10:49.080
Haven't you been in the summer yet?

00:10:49.620 --> 00:10:53.880
Did you hear about it yesterday?

00:10:54.120 --> 00:10:56.210
Idiot. It was just a coincidence.

00:10:56.610 --> 00:10:57.770
Oh...

00:10:57.770 --> 00:10:59.880
So, how was it after that?

00:11:00.410 --> 00:11:01.920
Eh? Well, that's...

00:11:01.920 --> 00:11:04.020
N-No, not yet!

00:11:04.360 --> 00:11:05.840
You're not going to tell me?

00:11:06.100 --> 00:11:06.500
Yes.

00:11:08.420 --> 00:11:10.010
You're not going to tell me?

00:11:10.290 --> 00:11:11.450
Huh...

00:11:11.450 --> 00:11:13.420
Um, is that all you want to hear?

00:11:15.200 --> 00:11:17.880
Your love story with Kuma-san...

00:11:17.880 --> 00:11:19.970
Ah, that's enough.

00:11:20.530 --> 00:11:22.820
Um, I want you to tell me something, too.

00:11:22.820 --> 00:11:25.540
Um, please play a match with me!

00:11:25.900 --> 00:11:29.620
Kuma-san, at that time...

00:11:30.090 --> 00:11:30.970
It was natural for him to say no.

00:11:31.270 --> 00:11:34.380
But from now on, I'm going to be a professional, too.

00:11:34.480 --> 00:11:35.870
I'm going to keep playing games that I can't really lose to.

00:11:36.630 --> 00:11:38.650
Just like Takuma-san,

00:11:38.930 --> 00:11:41.170
I have to get results in a game that took my life.

00:11:43.250 --> 00:11:44.550
So please give me just one match.

00:11:45.990 --> 00:11:50.890
So Kiku,

00:11:51.030 --> 00:11:53.150
Do you think you can beat me now?

00:11:53.750 --> 00:11:56.030
I don't know.

00:11:56.270 --> 00:11:58.500
But if I can't beat Takuma-san,

00:11:58.580 --> 00:11:58.680
I have to win.

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:00.900
I don't think I'll be able to do it.

00:12:01.750 --> 00:12:06.250
I see. Then I'll do it.

00:12:06.510 --> 00:12:07.690
What? Really?

00:12:08.250 --> 00:12:14.130
Well, I just want to beat you to death right now.

00:12:17.290 --> 00:12:19.310
Come to the first court if you feel like it.

00:12:19.470 --> 00:12:29.960
Hey, Takuma. Sorry, but...

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:30.420
I'm counting on you.

00:12:30.600 --> 00:12:33.140
Hello, Aoi-san.

00:12:33.260 --> 00:12:34.740
At this point, just do it.

00:12:36.200 --> 00:12:37.540
Who's your ally?

00:12:38.620 --> 00:12:42.420
Takuma is now in the 500th place in the world.

00:12:42.420 --> 00:12:44.000
It's a momentum that goes over in a blink of an eye.

00:12:45.680 --> 00:12:46.200
500?

00:12:46.620 --> 00:12:50.360
Even Alex is in the 890th place in the world.

00:12:50.500 --> 00:12:53.840
3 set match. Takuma service play.

00:12:54.120 --> 00:12:56.940
A year and a half ago, I didn't even know how far away he was.

00:12:57.940 --> 00:12:59.700
But now...

00:13:00.570 --> 00:13:03.450
You can't let that happen. I'm growing up too.

00:13:03.490 --> 00:13:06.680
Believe in yourself, and sharpen your instincts!

00:13:07.730 --> 00:13:08.070
Huh?!

00:13:09.790 --> 00:13:10.710
Fifteen Love!

00:13:10.910 --> 00:13:12.600
What the hell?!

00:13:13.720 --> 00:13:14.420
Thirty Love!

00:13:14.600 --> 00:13:16.620
I can't believe I've been served so many times!

00:13:17.340 --> 00:13:18.800
Ah! That was fast!

00:13:19.000 --> 00:13:19.880
Forty Love!

00:13:20.410 --> 00:13:23.020
Whoa! That's more than I expected.

00:13:23.500 --> 00:13:26.110
If you call a newborn's physical ability a talent,

00:13:26.830 --> 00:13:28.930
there's no one else who's been blessed with such a talent.

00:13:30.760 --> 00:13:33.700
I was a little nervous at times, but if I could get something out of it, I'd do this much.

00:13:39.900 --> 00:13:41.700
Game Takuma 1-0.

00:13:42.200 --> 00:13:44.160
Can you break something like this?

00:13:44.660 --> 00:13:47.840
No, that kind of negative thinking is no good.

00:13:48.080 --> 00:13:48.970
All I have to do is keep the serve.

00:13:49.970 --> 00:13:59.280
The shot is deep, and when it's shallow, be careful of the course.

00:14:03.640 --> 00:14:07.490
But I've experienced this weight in Florida.

00:14:08.190 --> 00:14:08.630
Hey.

00:14:15.590 --> 00:14:16.490
Fifteen love.

00:14:16.650 --> 00:14:16.910
Okay.

00:14:17.700 --> 00:14:20.700
The control I got in Florida is working for Takuma.

00:14:21.500 --> 00:14:24.330
So you can attack without waiting for a chance.

00:14:25.650 --> 00:14:28.740
Well, it's been two years since I came to the top of my junior high school.

00:14:30.570 --> 00:14:32.370
I didn't think you were talented in any way.

00:14:33.050 --> 00:14:34.180
Tae-chan!

00:14:34.440 --> 00:14:35.830
Did you decide to do tennis?

00:14:36.290 --> 00:14:39.140
Oh, I haven't applied yet.

00:14:41.060 --> 00:14:42.650
What are you?

00:14:42.790 --> 00:14:44.640
Is Sakuma-senpai also aiming to be a professional?

00:14:45.580 --> 00:14:46.100
Professional?

00:14:47.350 --> 00:14:47.530
What?

00:14:47.790 --> 00:14:49.930
Is there a connection?

00:14:50.790 --> 00:14:52.380
So, for the time being, I'll try to do it at the limit.

00:14:53.400 --> 00:14:56.740
To be honest, he was a guy who made people angry.

00:14:57.540 --> 00:14:59.680
This is a great scene.

00:15:00.020 --> 00:15:01.240
I have to admit the speed of evolution.

00:15:01.420 --> 00:15:03.880
The speed of evolution...

00:15:04.130 --> 00:15:05.330
He was like that too.

00:15:06.600 --> 00:15:07.540
Go, Sochi!

00:15:10.160 --> 00:15:12.760
I thought there was no big difference between the talent I had and the one I was born with.

00:15:14.220 --> 00:15:17.040
However, I was overtaken in a blink of an eye.

00:15:17.320 --> 00:15:24.030
I've been told that I have talent, but it doesn't make much sense.

00:15:24.350 --> 00:15:28.890
After all, I'm fine with you, but what I have is different.

00:15:30.120 --> 00:15:31.920
It's just a matter of whether or not you can live with it.

00:15:32.260 --> 00:15:33.510
What is it?

00:15:33.670 --> 00:15:35.140
Fifteen All.

00:15:35.400 --> 00:15:39.080
Hey, are you going to play again?

00:15:39.500 --> 00:15:41.220
It's the national championship soon.

00:15:41.560 --> 00:15:43.330
I see. Do your best.

00:15:43.630 --> 00:15:47.610
Game Takuma. 5-2. Takuma leads.

00:15:47.990 --> 00:15:52.430
What made Takuma be able to win as a professional recently is the absence of a serve.

00:15:53.090 --> 00:15:57.230
Yeah. I loved a serve that I couldn't stop practicing even when it was rotten.

00:15:57.770 --> 00:15:59.880
In the professional world, how much...

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:03.850
I thought it was a very important shot, but I finally realized it.

00:16:04.010 --> 00:16:09.500
That's why I finally got used to the big servers in Japan.

00:16:09.620 --> 00:16:15.320
My serve game is easy to take advantage of the return, so I can't control it.

00:16:15.880 --> 00:16:19.280
Takuma-san is a powerful serve, so I can decide easily.

00:16:19.360 --> 00:16:24.510
Game count 52. The difference in the score is the difference in the serve.

00:16:24.670 --> 00:16:28.000
I want that kind of serve too.

00:16:31.850 --> 00:16:39.140
If you want to fight at a professional level, even if you don't have the power or confidence, a strong serve is a necessary condition.

00:16:39.440 --> 00:16:50.450
I was very strong. Did you notice that?

00:16:50.530 --> 00:16:58.700
I shouldn't have put too much effort into this. The rhythm of the stroke is important. I should have a high score.

00:17:00.830 --> 00:17:01.250
What!?

00:17:02.740 --> 00:17:04.840
Double fault, love 15!

00:17:05.220 --> 00:17:10.060
Oh, I should've used more rhythm and used a little bit of the previous hit...

00:17:11.090 --> 00:17:14.020
Fault!

00:17:14.180 --> 00:17:15.860
I can't do this at all...

00:17:15.860 --> 00:17:19.660
I can't win this match if my serve doesn't evolve...

00:17:20.060 --> 00:17:22.280
Double fault, love 30!

00:17:22.640 --> 00:17:26.090
Hey, hey, are you going to throw away this game with your serve practice?

00:17:27.050 --> 00:17:29.810
Considering the possibility of winning, the course...

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:30.780
There's no other way, right?

00:17:31.680 --> 00:17:35.630
I wanted you to notice that, but it's too much to notice.

00:17:35.670 --> 00:17:36.810
I'm in trouble again.

00:17:37.470 --> 00:17:40.430
Double fault love 40

00:17:40.430 --> 00:17:44.710
I'm not tall and I don't have the power.

00:17:44.750 --> 00:17:46.680
I have no choice but to cover it with efficient body movements.

00:17:51.660 --> 00:17:56.620
Double fault first set won by Takuma.

00:17:56.730 --> 00:17:58.270
Count 6-2

00:17:58.270 --> 00:17:59.860
Little by little.

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:03.320
But it's getting better. I wanted to hit more, but I can't help it.

00:18:04.260 --> 00:18:07.660
I'll write down what I've learned in my notebook and remember it in my mind.

00:18:07.680 --> 00:18:10.040
So that I can move my instincts as soon as possible.

00:18:10.420 --> 00:18:10.820
Time!

00:18:11.910 --> 00:18:12.690
Return game.

00:18:13.500 --> 00:18:15.660
First of all, I'll look at that serve carefully and return it.

00:18:17.350 --> 00:18:18.830
Always the same rhythm toss.

00:18:19.860 --> 00:18:23.060
At the same time, the knee bends and the lower body gains strength.

00:18:23.140 --> 00:18:27.740
The moment the knee stretches, the power of the lower body is released.

00:18:27.940 --> 00:18:29.320
Just after that, the shoulder swings.

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:33.310
The power is the elbow that is like a whip from the shoulder.

00:18:33.670 --> 00:18:36.230
While the wrist and racket are intensified,

00:18:36.390 --> 00:18:41.460
the highest point that is the most intensified in the upper body is the impact.

00:18:42.330 --> 00:18:45.710
I'm completely fascinated.

00:18:47.560 --> 00:18:48.020
I can see it.

00:18:52.380 --> 00:18:55.200
Out 30 Love

00:18:55.200 --> 00:18:57.050
I'll see it more often.

00:18:57.370 --> 00:18:59.620
Like a whip.

00:19:00.120 --> 00:19:00.460
I'll be the one to lose.

00:19:01.120 --> 00:19:04.760
I'm out.

00:19:05.160 --> 00:19:06.120
40 Love.

00:19:06.240 --> 00:19:08.090
I'll be back in a bit.

00:19:08.430 --> 00:19:10.180
I'm coming back.

00:19:10.400 --> 00:19:14.840
Oh, by the way, that was when a one-month-old amateur

00:19:14.840 --> 00:19:16.470
started to eat up my serve.

00:19:17.910 --> 00:19:20.790
He's a guy who makes me so angry.

00:19:20.790 --> 00:19:21.690
You're such a pain in the ass!

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:31.040
Takuma 1-0

00:19:31.040 --> 00:19:33.990
With the help of Takuma-san's serve that burned in my eyes

00:19:33.990 --> 00:19:36.590
How will I hit my body?

00:19:36.690 --> 00:19:42.070
I'm going to make you die

00:19:42.070 --> 00:19:44.260
I did it!

00:19:44.260 --> 00:19:46.430
Asahi!

00:19:46.470 --> 00:19:46.910
I'll aim!

00:19:47.110 --> 00:19:50.140
Balloon!

00:19:51.660 --> 00:19:52.660
Fifteen Love

00:19:52.660 --> 00:19:53.160
Alright!

00:19:53.650 --> 00:19:55.950
Not yet

00:19:56.390 --> 00:19:56.590
Faster!

00:19:57.170 --> 00:19:57.510
Ah!

00:20:00.220 --> 00:20:00.680
It's not bad.

00:20:00.820 --> 00:20:02.680
The second is just as it is.

00:20:08.260 --> 00:20:11.420
The second serve of Hayase is no good.

00:20:11.600 --> 00:20:14.510
The game will change up to here with just the serve.

00:20:14.510 --> 00:20:16.200
A faster serve.

00:20:16.340 --> 00:20:18.280
Not only the elbow and wrist,

00:20:18.780 --> 00:20:19.530
but also the waist.

00:20:20.640 --> 00:20:22.680
Like a single whip for the whole body.

00:20:26.640 --> 00:20:27.680
All right!

00:20:28.300 --> 00:20:28.740
Oh!

00:20:31.310 --> 00:20:33.500
I can't speed up on the second serve.

00:20:33.560 --> 00:20:35.420
I'll spin as hard as I can!

00:20:35.420 --> 00:20:36.540
I'll try to get it on!

00:20:36.540 --> 00:20:37.260
I'll make it safe!

00:20:37.680 --> 00:20:37.920
Oh!

00:20:38.670 --> 00:20:38.970
Ugh!

00:20:39.210 --> 00:20:39.870
I missed the timing!

00:20:40.350 --> 00:20:40.470
Ugh!

00:20:40.730 --> 00:20:46.020
Straight or drop shot?

00:20:48.900 --> 00:20:49.840
30 All!

00:20:50.060 --> 00:20:50.750
Takuma!

00:20:50.890 --> 00:20:52.980
I told you to limit your drop shots to when you're at a higher level!

00:20:54.360 --> 00:20:56.740
A painful shot is a habit!

00:20:57.220 --> 00:20:58.300
I knew it!

00:20:58.800 --> 00:20:59.710
I knew it!

00:21:00.250 --> 00:21:01.070
That was a shot he missed.

00:21:01.790 --> 00:21:03.590
He's standing up for himself on the serve.

00:21:03.750 --> 00:21:06.150
He can do it. Next time, he'll use a fast serve.

00:21:07.040 --> 00:21:07.880
Hey, stop!

00:21:08.400 --> 00:21:08.780
Huh?

00:21:09.970 --> 00:21:13.310
Let's call it quits for this match.

00:21:13.630 --> 00:21:17.700
What? What are you saying all of a sudden?

00:21:18.320 --> 00:21:20.060
Sorry, I meant to say quits.

00:21:21.160 --> 00:21:21.680
Why?

00:21:22.690 --> 00:21:25.680
If you keep this up, you're likely to get injured.

00:21:27.220 --> 00:21:27.740
Huh?

00:21:28.130 --> 00:21:29.600
Akuma-san!

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:31.940
Wait a minute! I'm not injured at all!

00:21:32.540 --> 00:21:36.080
It can't be helped. If Aoi-san says so...

00:21:36.780 --> 00:21:40.550
And it's not a stop, it's a stop.

00:21:40.950 --> 00:21:46.080
I'm not in a good mood either. I'll do the rest at any time.

00:21:47.490 --> 00:21:49.670
Sorry, I asked you to do it from here.

00:21:49.850 --> 00:21:52.380
No, thank you for your hard work.

00:21:52.740 --> 00:21:55.230
Hey, Aoi-coach!

00:21:55.470 --> 00:21:58.550
Well, calm down. I'll explain it properly.

00:22:30.796 --> 00:22:31.796
As expected

00:24:00.600 --> 00:24:01.660
Oh, it's Shumitsu-san.

00:24:01.860 --> 00:24:02.520
You know her?

00:24:03.340 --> 00:24:05.890
Yeah, she's the first girl of this year.

00:24:06.330 --> 00:24:09.430
She's won 4 times in these 3 years, but she's never won once.

00:24:09.890 --> 00:24:11.210
Nacchan has won 4 times?

00:24:11.770 --> 00:24:14.620
If possible, I want to win once before I become a professional.

00:24:14.820 --> 00:24:15.670
I didn't know.

00:24:16.440 --> 00:24:19.300
Nacchan had a partner like Nabai-kun for me.

00:24:20.070 --> 00:24:22.240
Next time on Baby Step,

00:24:22.460 --> 00:24:23.250
The first encounter with the police!
